    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe refactor is structurally clean and idiomatic:\n\n- **Logic lives in the right unit.** The holiday calendar is a private `static final Set` constant inside the one class that normalizes the date \u2014 no premature extraction of a \"HolidayService\" the spec doesn't call for, and no leaking the concern elsewhere.\n- **The right abstraction emerged.** Replacing the two hard-coded Saturday/Sunday branches with a single `isBusinessDay(LocalDate)` predicate plus a roll-forward loop is exactly the generalization the spec implies. Weekend and holiday are now expressed as one coherent \"is this a valid day\" concept rather than two parallel mechanisms, and the loop naturally handles runs of consecutive non-business days (weekend abutting a holiday) without special-casing.\n- **No duplication, no catch-all.** The class still does one thing; the new helper is small, well-named, and `private static` (correctly, since it needs no instance state).\n- **Docstring kept in sync** with the behavior change, including the derived-values note.\n\nThis reads like code a maintainer of this codebase would have written.",
